      ]
    },
    "description": "OrderGateway exposes a shared CommandMailbox to several HTTP request threads, a scheduler thread, and a command-processing worker. Request handlers submit CompleteOrder and CancelOrder commands and await their individual results. The worker removes commands one at a time, so when the mailbox is empty it cannot execute another command immediately and later discover one. A command submitted while the worker is idle must eventually be processed rather than being rejected, because the HTTP request remains outstanding until the business operation completes. Incoming commands may also need to wait for a per-order authorization record to appear, which another component supplies after a database callback. The mailbox must preserve FIFO ordering, wake the worker exactly when work arrives, avoid lost notifications, and ensure that a worker stopping does not strand a producer. Callers are not permitted to spin while waiting, and a timeout must report failure without corrupting command state.",
    "decision_statement": "What should a mailbox operation do when the worker cannot currently proceed, given that the submitted command must eventually be processed?",
    "notes": "Guarded-suspension fits suspending mailbox operations until work or authorization arrives instead of refusing; monitor-object and lockable-object are near-misses (owned synchronization, published locks), supported by thread-safe-interface and two-phase-termination for worker shutdown."
  },
